  "summary": "Published items cluster on macrophage, T cell and dendritic cell roles in lung, heart, kidney and joint fibrosis, plus one PDGFA niche preprint in alveolar…",
  "synthesis": "Activity is concentrated in published studies (16 items, one preprint) that place immune cells at the center of fibrotic remodeling. Reported mechanisms include CCR2+ monocyte AXL signalling through MEK/ERK in radiation-induced cardiac fibrosis, PD1+ T cells acting via CXCL9/CXCR3 after myocardial infarction, and doxorubicin-reprogrammed CD8+ T cells stiffening cardiac matrix via LOX. MMP12 drives fibrogenic macrophages in granuloma-associated cardiac fibrosis, while SPP1+ macrophages recur in pulmonary fibrosis multi-omics and in osteoarthritis synovial niche work. Single-cell censuses of pulmonary endarterectomy tissue and MSC-driven repair of cDC2 OXPHOS defects in systemic sclerosis extend the immune framing. The rise ratio of 2.5 is reported alongside these 16 published items, with no code, industry or star signals recorded, so the drivers of growth are not characterized here.",
